ckly move this rating.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Georgia remains one of the tightest states on the presidential map. Its partisan lean favors Republicans by roughly a point, and with no incumbent on either side, the contest starts close to even. No public polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet for 2028, so the outlook leans on fundamentals alone.\n\nRecent headlines point to Democratic energy in the state: Jon Ossoff's commanding 2026 race and a closely watched governor's contest have fueled talk of shifting margins. But midterm strength does not always transfer to presidential elections, and the state's recent top-of-ticket results have narrowly favored Republicans. Until actual 2028 polling arrives, Georgia is best treated as a genuine toss-up with a slight Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4567, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4683, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.467, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4627, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4625, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4629, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4605, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4643, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4656, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.455, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4633, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4576, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-